{"name":"Atlas Cedar","hex":"#5ca0a7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"atlas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bound collection of maps often including tables, illustrations or other text.","A bound collection of tables, illustrations, etc. on any given subject."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich satin fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atlas"},{"term":"cedar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coniferous tree of the genus Cedrus in the family Pinaceae.","A coniferous tree of the family Cupressaceae, especially of the genera Juniperus, Cupressus, Calocedrus, or Thuja."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cedar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cedrus atlantica","blocks":[{"text":"Cedrus atlantica, the Atlas cedar, is a species of coniferous tree in the pine family Pinaceae, native to the Rif and Atlas Mountains of Morocco, and to the Tell Atlas in Algeria. A majority of the modern sources treat it as a distinct species Cedrus atlantica, but some sources consider it a subspecies of Lebanon cedar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Cedrus_atlantica.jpg/330px-Cedrus_atlantica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedrus_atlantica","wikidata":"Q623489"},{"title":"Atlas","blocks":[{"text":"An atlas is a collection of maps; it is typically a bundle of maps of Earth or of a continent or region of Earth. Advances in astronomy have also resulted in atlases of the celestial sphere or of other planets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Mercator_-_Atlas_-_1595.png/330px-Mercator_-_Atlas_-_1595.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlas","wikidata":"Q162827"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Cedrus_libani_ssp._atlantica_%27Glauca%27_cone_0